   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 8,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "title": "How to use - tested on RTX 3060",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## How to use - tested on RTX 3060 12 GB\n\nNeeds the node pack **comfyui-viggle-animate-h3** (Comfy registry; its GitHub repo was offline on 2026-09-29).\n\n1. Driving video: the motion, camera, background and light come from here. Cut it to 24 fps; 124 frames = 5.2 s.\n2. Character: ONE still. Best: repaint the first frame of the driving video (same pose + framing) with an image-edit model.\n3. Press **Run**. The result keeps the driving clip's audio.\n\nMeasured on the 3060: the mouth follows the timing of the speech but opens less than the original (see the repo README)."
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "## How to use - tested on RTX 3060 12 GB\n\nNeeds the node pack **comfyui-viggle-animate-h3** (Comfy registry; its GitHub repo was offline on 2026-09-29).\n\n1. Driving video: the motion, camera, background and light come from here. Cut it to 24 fps; 124 frames = 5.2 s.\n2. Character: ONE still. Best: repaint the first frame of the driving video (same pose + framing) with an image-edit model.\n3. Press **Run**. The result keeps the driving clip's audio.\n\nMeasured on the 3060: the mouth follows the timing of the speech but opens less than the original (see the repo README)."
   },
